   Note: The gossip validation in validateBeaconBlockPubSub only checks: blob count, slot timing, parent known/finalized, proposer index, proposer signature, and Bellatrix-specific (timestamp + parent-optimistic). It does NOT check individual transaction sizes within the execution payload. Transaction-level validation (including per-tx gas caps from EIP-7825) is performed by the execution engine (EL) via newPayload calls, not in the consensus layer gossip validation. Private channel transactions (Flashbots Protect etc.) that include oversized transactions would be caught when the EL processes the payload via newPayload, not at gossip validation time.
